<h2 id="criteria-section-introduction" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="05XF">97.1</span> Introduction</h2>

<p>
The purpose of this chapter is to find criteria guaranteeing that a stack in groupoids over the category of schemes with the fppf topology is an algebraic stack. Historically, this often involved proving that certain functors were representable, see Grothendieck's lectures <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Gr-I">Gr-I</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Gr-II">Gr-II</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Gr-III">Gr-III</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Gr-IV">Gr-IV</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Gr-V">Gr-V</a>]</span>, and <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Gr-VI">Gr-VI</a>]</span>. This explains the title of this chapter. Another important source of this material comes from the work of Artin, see <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/ArtinI">ArtinI</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/ArtinII">ArtinII</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Artin-Theorem-Representability">Artin-Theorem-Representability</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Artin-Construction-Techniques">Artin-Construction-Techniques</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Artin-Algebraic-Spaces">Artin-Algebraic-Spaces</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Artin-Algebraic-Approximation">Artin-Algebraic-Approximation</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Artin-Implicit-Function">Artin-Implicit-Function</a>]</span>, and <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/ArtinVersal">ArtinVersal</a>]</span>. 
</p>
